    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6502250b-62e0-5514-ae60-fb4f5a71ad76",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gioachino Rossini, Andrea Leone Tottola, Francesco Ringhieri, Gaetano Donizetti, Sonia Ganassi, Richard Mohr, Samuel Barber, Gian Carlo Menotti\n- Works: Mosè in Egitto, L'Osiride, Lucrezia Borgia, Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra, La donna del lago, Ermione, Vanessa, Amahl and the Night Visitors, Ernani, Luisa Miller, Rigoletto, Aida, La Traviata, Il Trovatore\n- Organizations/Events: ROF, Rossini in Wildbad\n- Concepts: opera, libretto, play, LP recording\n\nFacts:\n- Francesco Ringhieri wrote the 1760 play L'Osiride.\n- Mosè in Egitto is a three-act opera by Gioachino Rossini with an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola based on Francesco Ringhieri's play L'Osiride.\n- Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\n- Richard Mohr produced recordings of the world-premiere casts of Samuel Barber's Vanessa and Gian Carlo Menotti's Amahl and the Night Visitors.\n- Richard Mohr also produced the first LP recordings of Ernani, Luisa Miller, and Lucrezia Borgia, and three versions each of Rigoletto, Aida, La Traviata, and Il Trovatore.\n- Sonia Ganassi sang Elisabetta in Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra at ROF in 2004.\n- Sonia Ganassi sang Elena in La donna del lago at Rossini in Wildbad in 2006.\n- Sonia Ganassi performed in Ermione at ROF in 2008.\n- Sonia Ganassi sang Elcia in Mosè in Egitto at ROF in 2011.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "600c5d05-8a4f-5867-8268-a7220b13bfe1",
        "text": "Page: Mosè in Egitto. Sentence: Mosè in Egitto (\"Moses in Egypt)\" (] ) is a three-act opera written by Gioachino Rossini to an Italian libretto by Andrea Leone Tottola, which was based on a 1760 play by Francesco Ringhieri, \"L'Osiride\".\nPage: Lucrezia Borgia (opera). Sentence: Lucrezia Borgia is a melodramatic opera in a prologue and two acts by Gaetano Donizetti.\nPage: Sonia Ganassi. Sentence: Her roles in Rossini operas include Elisabetta in \"Elisabetta, regina d'Inghilterra\" (ROF, 2004), Elena in \"La donna del lago (Lady of the Lake)\" (Rossini in Wildbad, 2006), \"Ermione\" (ROF, 2008), and Elcia in \"Mosè in Egitto\" (ROF, 2011).\nPage: Richard Mohr. Sentence: His producing credits included recording the casts of the world premieres of Samuel Barber's \"Vanessa\" and Gian Carlo Menotti's \"Amahl and the Night Visitors,\" as well as the first LP recordings of \"Ernani,\" \"Luisa Miller\" and \"Lucrezia Borgia\" and three versions each of \"Rigoletto,\" \"Aida,\" \"La Traviata\" and \"Il Trovatore.\"",
